config OPENBMC_PHOSPHOR_STATE_MANAGER
    bool "openbmc phosphor state manager"
    select OPENBMC_SDBUSPLUS
    select OPENBMC_PHOSPHOR_DBUS_INTERFACES
    select OPENBMC_PHOSPHOR_LOGGING
    select OPENBMC_FMT
    select OPENBMC_CEREAL
    select CPP_EXCEPTIONS
    help
      Enable the phosphor-state-manager daemons (BMC / Host / Chassis /
      Hypervisor state) on Zephyr.

      NOTE: this is a port of the upstream meson project. Each daemon is
      compiled as a separate object set but all of them run as Zephyr
      threads inside the single BMC application; each *_main() entry point
      connects to the in-process dbus-broker with connect_to_dbroker()
      instead of sdbusplus::bus::new_default().

if OPENBMC_PHOSPHOR_STATE_MANAGER

config OPENBMC_PHOSPHOR_STATE_MANAGER_BMC
    bool "BMC state manager (xyz.openbmc_project.State.BMC)"
    default y
    help
      Owns /xyz/openbmc_project/state/bmc0 and exposes CurrentBMCState,
      RequestedBMCTransition, LastRebootTime and LastRebootCause.

      On Zephyr there is no systemd, so the BMC state is *always* reported
      as Ready once this daemon has started; the reboot cause cannot be
      read from a watchdog bootstatus sysfs file and is reported as
      Unknown (see bmc_state_manager.cpp).

config OPENBMC_PHOSPHOR_STATE_MANAGER_HOST
    bool "Host state manager (xyz.openbmc_project.State.Host)"
    default n
    help
      Owns /xyz/openbmc_project/state/host0. Requires the ObjectMapper and
      (for the auto-reboot policy) the settings daemon; without them the
      daemon still starts but the power-restore policy lookups fail.
      Still experimental on Zephyr -- enable only when completing the
      host sub-application.

config OPENBMC_PHOSPHOR_STATE_MANAGER_CHASSIS
    bool "Chassis state manager (xyz.openbmc_project.State.Chassis)"
    default n
    help
      Owns /xyz/openbmc_project/state/chassis0 and the PowerOnHours
      counter. Uses an sdeventplus timer for the POH increment.
      Still experimental on Zephyr -- enable only when completing the
      chassis sub-application.

config OPENBMC_PHOSPHOR_STATE_MANAGER_HYPERVISOR
    bool "Hypervisor state manager (xyz.openbmc_project.State.Hypervisor)"
    default n
    help
      Owns /xyz/openbmc_project/state/hypervisor0 and mirrors the host
      BootProgress property. Still experimental on Zephyr.

endif # OPENBMC_PHOSPHOR_STATE_MANAGER
